5. **Extraction**: Run the sample through the MS flow cell.
6. **Analysis**: Measure the signal produced by ionisation of the sputtered atoms.

\section{Precautions}
Handling radioactive materials requires strict adherence to safety protocols. Always work in a fume hood or decontamination chamber. Do not expose yourself to radiation fields during the extraction process.

\section{Conclusion}
Accurate measurement of stable isotopes allows researchers to distinguish between natural background radiation and anthropogenic contamination. This procedure follows established mass spectrometric workflows to ensure reliable data.
